# ASXL1-mutated fibroblasts — analysis summary (bix-5-q4)

## Assumption (explicit)
`condition == "disease"` is treated as ASXL1-mutated fibroblasts and `control` as WT
controls (approved assumption; the metadata file does not itself name the mutated gene).
Samples MGD1640F/MGD1641F (count columns without metadata) were dropped.

## Pipeline (executed in analysis_asxl1_fibro.py)
1. Counts read with whitespace separator (file is space-, not tab-separated): 60,662 genes x 16 samples -> 14 samples.
2. Ensembl -> HGNC approved symbol mapping (37,547 IDs via HGNC 05-09-19, rest gencode gene_name); duplicate symbols summed -> 59,087 genes.
3. Filter: CPM > 1 in >= 7 samples -> 13,747 genes tested.
4. Normalisation: DESeq2-style median-of-ratios size factors. PCA: PC2 cleanly separates disease vs control.
5. DE: DESeq2-style negative-binomial GLM (method-of-moments dispersion shrunk to a robust mean-dispersion trend, Wald test), model ~condition; sensitivity model ~condition+sex (Spearman rho of LFC = 0.948; 532/683 sig genes shared).
   - FDR<0.05: 683 significant; 370 up / 190 down (|log2FC|>0.58); 199 up / 119 down at |log2FC|>1.
6. Enrichment (SURROGATE - offline environment has no R/gseapy/goatools/GO annotation):
   15 GO-branch-guided curated gene sets; hypergeometric ORA + pre-ranked GSEA
   (gene-label permutation, 2000 perms, BH-corrected).
7. Sensitivity: limma-style empirical-Bayes moderated t on log2CPM (Smyth d0=6.5):
   70 up / 19 down DE genes, all contained in the NB-GLM lists (70/70, 19/19);
   rank correlation with NB z = 0.957; GSEA re-run on limma t reproduces the same
   DOWN-direction ordering.

## Key results
- UP direction (higher in ASXL1-mutant): NO significantly enriched process.
  Best GSEA: chromatin organization & histone modification NES 1.26 (padj 0.14);
  best ORA: ECM organization & fibrosis padj 0.34.
- DOWN direction (lower in ASXL1-mutant) - consistently significant in ORA and both GSEA runs:
  * Cellular senescence & p53 signaling: ORA padj 0.0056 (5 hits, FE 8.0; hits IL6, TGM2, EGR1, JUNB, SNAI1);
    GSEA NES 1.98 (padj 0.0037; limma-t NES 2.06).  <-- strongest ORA + consistent GSEA
  * Response to oxidative & ER stress: GSEA NES 2.15 (padj 0.0025; limma-t NES 2.18)
  * Oxidative phosphorylation: GSEA NES 2.11 (limma-t NES 2.31)
  * Translation & ribosome biogenesis: GSEA NES 2.09 (limma-t NES 1.92)
  These four form one coherent suppressed program (senescence/SASP + metabolism + protein synthesis).

## Answer
The most enriched process in ASXL1-mutated fibroblasts is cellular senescence / p53 signaling,
and it is DOWN-regulated (suppressed) relative to controls (with parallel suppression of
oxidative phosphorylation, oxidative/ER-stress response and translation); no process is
significantly enriched among the up-regulated genes.

